# Advice printed when Step 1.5 hits: the doc sections to spot-check.
# One section per line, same grammar as doc-sensitive-paths; REPLACES the
# built-in defaults. Tailored alongside the path list, which upstream requires
# (gregoryfoster/skills#261) — the list says what the gate watches, this says
# what to do about a hit. Each line names the change that usually triggers it.
#
# LINE CONTRACT: every line reads `<tracked doc path>: <what to check>`. The
# leading path is what makes the advice auditable — tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py
# fails any line whose first `:`-delimited token is not a tracked file, so a
# section written as plain prose ("route table in AGENTS.md") is a test failure,
# not a silent no-op.
#
# Guarded by tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py.

AGENTS.md: the authoritative summary — conventions, watched-items rules, the detail-doc table (any structural change)
README.md: orientation and curated links only; the deep material belongs in docs/
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: module layout, sibling services, the single process (src/ layout, a new sibling or worker)
docs/BUS.md: broker ownership, the stream inventory, retention, consumer groups (new streams or consumers, maxlen changes)
docs/BUS-CONNECTION-POLICY.md: client timeouts, the zero-retry rule, URL redaction, the startup PING (src/core/bus.py, src/core/read_windows.py, any new blocking consumer)
docs/COMMANDS.md: every runnable command (scripts/, pyproject.toml scripts and deps)
docs/DEPENDENCIES.md: the wheelhouse and the notifier SDK's git tag — pins, auth, upgrade notes (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, scripts/sync_wheelhouse.py)
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md: systemd units, install runbook, timers (deploy/, tests/deploy/)
docs/HOST-MEMORY.md: the MemoryLow reservations, slice drop-ins, kernel reserve, the earlyoom decline (deploy/dropins/, deploy/watcher.service memory lines)
docs/ENVIRONMENT.md: env files, variables, the unit-only credentials (new config keys in src/core/config.py, deploy/)
docs/CO-INDEX.md: the shared-index client contract, the green-failing traps (.socraticode.json, .claude/settings.json env block)
docs/SOCRATICODE.md: index scope, .socraticodeignore entries, link stubs (.socraticodeignore, sibling checkouts)
docs/MIGRATIONS.md: manual upgrade steps, grants, one-time orderings (alembic/versions/)
docs/REGISTRY.md: what an announcement owns, every reconcile 409, linkage (src/workers/registry_reconcile.py, announcement-owned columns)
docs/WATCHED-ITEMS.md: fields, schedule resolution, notifications (src/core/watched_items.py, notifications)
docs/WATCHED-ITEMS-DASHBOARD.md: routes, lifecycle guards, list and detail views (src/dashboard/)
